      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "RULING DAME (5) is the clear horse to beat, with her Kalgoorlie third two starts back reading strongly for this after she led and was only collared late by Lord Momo in a CL2. Her latest second-last can be treated with caution after she raced wide throughout and keenly, and the quick back-up plus a more suitable assignment give her the right platform to rebound. MAKE DE FORTUNE (4) also comes back from provincial CL2 company and was only beaten two and a half lengths at Kalgoorlie despite being unwanted in the market, so she profiles as the main danger if she repeats that effort. DANEA ROCK (3) has placed at both runs since resuming and brings reliable place form, though her long maiden record keeps the winning case in check. BLOWIN' SMOKE (2) worked home into third at Mingenew and has won at this venue, but the first try around 1600m can see him continue his run of recent form. WHO'S YOUR MAMA (1) can be in the finish stepping out in distance.",
